Z||000000||Hank is Here||10-01-2000||10:54 PM||||The temp gauge is has not been working on my 87 GT for a month or two.  I have not had time to find the problem recently but now should have time to trace the problem.  What are the likely culprits of the gauge needle not moving little or at all?  I did have time to do a quick test of the thermostat and it is working properly.  Where is the temp sensor in the block, what type of voltage should I be getting to the gauge?  Are there any common problems with the temp gauge?   Also, is there an idiot light as well as the gauge as a backup system? <P>Thanks <BR>Mark Johnson  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||10-01-2000||11:11 PM||||I'm not sure on the V6 model, but on the L4 there is a sensor located on the top of the cylinder head on the far back left hand side with two wires, one for the gauge and the other for the "idiot light". This is NOT the sensor on the back side of the head with one wire for the coolant fan or the ECM coolant temp switch located on the thermostat housing.||||reg||1
